    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CH-02 \u2014 Verify the website gap\n\n**This is the workflow the project stands or falls on.**\n\nCH-01 produces candidates. A candidate is a business whose Google Maps listing carries no website field. That is *not* the same as a business without a website, and the entire value of the lead list depends on the difference.\n\n### The five stages, cheapest first\n\n| | Stage | Costs | Catches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A | What did the listing claim? | free | social-only, Linktree, dead `business.site` |\n| B | Cross-check Overture + Foursquare | **free, unlimited** | the owner has a site, just never added it to Maps |\n| C | Search for them | ~$0.001 | a site under a name we would never guess |\n| D | Guess a domain and **prove** it | free | the rest |\n| E | PageSpeed | free | a site that exists but is unusable |\n| F | Find a contact email | free | only possible for HAS_WEBSITE / WEAK_WEBSITE - a confirmed no-website lead has nowhere for this to look, which is why outreach for those defaults to phone |\n\nEach stage that *completes* adds confidence. Each stage that cannot run leaves it lower. That is the whole mechanism:\n\n> **\"We checked and found nothing\" and \"we could not check\" must never produce the same number.**\n\n### Why there are no IF branches here\n\nEvery stage skips itself when an earlier one already settled the question. The flow stays linear, so there are no Merge nodes and no item-pairing bugs \u2014 the failure mode where one business's answer gets attached to another business.\n\nStage B re-pairs **by place id, not by position**, for the same reason.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Load the reference data first \u2014 Stage B is worthless against empty tables:\n   ```\n   python tools/load_overture.py --city Oslo --country Norway\n   python tools/load_fsq.py --city Oslo --country Norway\n   ```\n2. Optional: a Serper key in `Config` enables Stage C. Without it the pipeline still works, but confidence caps lower and fewer leads reach CONFIRMED. That is correct behaviour, not a bug.\n3. Optional: a PageSpeed key raises the rate limit. The API works without one.\n\n### Read this number in the report\n\n**\"False positives caught\"** \u2014 businesses whose listing said no website and which turned out to have one. Every one of those is an email that would have opened *\"I noticed you don't have a website\"* to somebody who does. If that number is zero on a batch of 20+, check the reference tables are actually populated for that city.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "ch02-sticky",
      "name": "What this is",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1520,
        100
      ]
    }
